# Shell scripts are checked out with LF endings on every platform.
#
# docker/entrypoint.sh is copied into a Linux container image and run by
# /bin/sh. A CRLF line ending makes the shebang line read as
# "#!/bin/sh\r", so the kernel looks for an interpreter whose name ends in
# a carriage return and the container exits immediately with a "no such
# file or directory" that names a file which plainly exists. Windows
# clones with core.autocrlf=true produce exactly that, so the ending is
# pinned here rather than left to a contributor's local git configuration.
*.sh text eol=lf
